#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""zidev — a cmux-style sidebar of Claude Code sessions, grouped by project.

Runs on its own tmux server (socket "zidev"), so sessions keep running when the
terminal quits. Each session is a tmux window: sidebar pane on the left, Claude on the
right. Claude Code hooks report each session's status to ~/.zidev/status.

  zidev              start (restoring saved sessions) or attach
  zidev DIR          the same, showing DIR's project (its first session); a new project if it is none
  zidev start        start the server in the background, without attaching
  zidev new [DIR] [--prompt TEXT]   new session in DIR (default: current dir); TEXT is Claude's first message
  zidev rename-project [DIR] NAME   show a project under NAME ("" gives back the folder's name)
  zidev archive DIR / unarchive DIR   hide a project (its sessions stop) / bring it back
  zidev list [--json]  print sessions and their status
  zidev kill         stop the tmux server (sessions stay saved, restored on next start)
  zidev reload       load new zidev code into a running server (Claude sessions keep running)
  zidev app          put zidev.app (its own window and icon) into ~/Applications and open it
  zidev --version    print the version
  zidev doctor       check the setup: tools, hook settings, saved state
  zidev logs [-f]    show (or follow) the error log
  zidev selftest     run the end-to-end test on a throwaway tmux server
  zidev apptest      check the running zidev.app against spec.md (clicks, cmd-cmd) on a throwaway window
  zidev open FILE[:LINE] [--tab]   (inside zidev) show a file in the preview, or as a tab
"""

